* The DRAWN transmission gate, extracted with its parasitics.
*
* Source: layout/adc-top/parasitics/reports/20260806-230838-56be937/adc_tgate.para.spice
* (`klt extract --deck gf180mcu --parasitics --pdk`, asserted against
* layout/adc-top/parasitics/cells.json by run_extract_parasitics.py),
* post-processed by remediate_extracted.py --leaf, which promotes the
* anonymous Nwell net every PMOS body lands on to a `vnw` pin instead
* of tying it inside the cell. This deck wires that pin to vdd below --
* the single-well convention tb_switch_ron.spice's own header states.
*
* Device geometry is asserted equal on both sides before this file is
* written: nfet_03v3 W=10.0u L=0.28u, pfet_03v3 W=20.0u L=0.28u.
* ===========================================================================
* REMEDIATED extracted leaf cell -- NOT raw `klt extract` output.
* Produced by layout/adc-top/parasitics/remediate_extracted.py
* (remediate_leaf):
*   - 1 PMOS body terminal(s) on 1 anonymous Nwell net(s) promoted to a new
*     .SUBCKT pin 'vnw', so the instantiating testbench supplies the
*     well bias explicitly (local remediation of the klt PMOS-body gap;
*     upstream klayout-tools#555). No net is tied inside the cell.
*   - device geometry, connectivity and the parasitic RC ladder are untouched.
* See remediate_extracted.py's remediate_leaf() for provenance.
